                <p rendition="#flush">I. <hi rendition="#italic">Report by the Deputies</hi></p>
                <p>The Council heard the report submitted by the Acting Chairman of the Deputies
                    (See CFM(D) (46) (NY) 124th
                        Meeting).<anchor n="4" xml:id="d371-f1"/></p>
                <p>The question of the powers of the Provisional Council of Government was
                    re-examined and after a further exchange of views a redraft of the text on this
                    subject was provisionally <hi rendition="#italic">agreed</hi> (with a
                    reservation by the U.K. Delegate—see Annex), and was referred to the Deputies
                    for consideration together with the U.S. and U.K. proposals contained in
                    documents CFM(46) (NY) 22 and 23
                    respectively, the French draft instructions to the Governor and the special
                    question dealt with in the U.K. memorandum of August 29, 1946 (Doc. CFM (46)258).<anchor n="5" xml:id="d371-f2"/></p>
                <p rendition="#flush">II. <hi rendition="#italic">Questions Outstanding on the Peace
                        Treaties</hi><anchor n="6" xml:id="d371-f3"/></p>
                <p>The Council resumed consideration item by item of the list of unsettled questions
                    in the various Treaty texts.</p>
                <pb facs="1392" n="1368" xml:id="pg1368"/>
                <p>(1) <hi rendition="#italic">Settlement of Economic Disputes</hi></p>
                <p>It was <hi rendition="#italic">agreed</hi> to adopt the Soviet Delegation’s
                    proposal for this Article in the various treaties as modified by the original
                    U.S. amendment under which the Secretary-General of the United Nations instead
                    of the President of the International Court of Justice would nominate an
                    arbitrator. It was further <hi rendition="#italic">agreed</hi> that Article 72
                    in the Italian Treaty should also include paragraphs (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >b</hi>) to (<hi rendition="#italic">g</hi>) of the Conference
                    recommendation on this Article. Final formulation of the relevant texts was
                    entrusted to the Economic Experts.</p>
                <p>(2) <hi rendition="#italic">Enemy Assets in the Territory of the Allied and
                        Associated Powers</hi></p>
                <p>It was <hi rendition="#italic">agreed</hi> to bring the text of Article 25 in the
                    Hungarian Treaty into line with that of the corresponding Article in the
                    Roumanian Treaty.</p>
                <p>The decision regarding Article 24 of the Bulgarian Treaty was <hi
                        rendition="#italic">deferred.</hi></p>
                <p>(3) <hi rendition="#italic">Return of Jewish Property</hi></p>
                <p>It was <hi rendition="#italic">agreed</hi> to accept the first paragraphs of
                    Article 24A of the Roumanian Treaty, and of Article 23A of the Hungarian Treaty
                    subject to the substitution of “fair compensation” for “full compensation”, and
                    to defer decision on the second paragraphs of those Articles.</p>
                <p>(4) <hi rendition="#italic">Rail Traffic</hi></p>
                <p>The Paris Conference recommendations for the texts of Article 28 bis in the
                    Bulgarian and Article 29 bis in the Hungarian Treaty were <hi
                        rendition="#italic">adopted.</hi></p>
                <p>(5) <hi rendition="#italic">Fair Prices for Reparation Deliveries</hi></p>
                <p>Decision <hi rendition="#italic">deferred.</hi></p>
                <p>(6) <hi rendition="#italic">Danube-Sava-Adriatic Railway</hi></p>
                <p>It was <hi rendition="#italic">agreed</hi> to accept the text of Article 23,
                    para. 9 of the Hungarian Treaty in the same wording as Annex III, para. 10 of
                    the Italian Treaty (See Doc. CFM (46)
                        (NY)30).<anchor n="7" xml:id="d371-f4"/></p>
                <p>(7) <hi rendition="#italic">Shipping</hi></p>
                <p>Decision <hi rendition="#italic">deferred.</hi></p>
                <p>(8) <hi rendition="#italic">Interpretation</hi></p>
                <p>Decision <hi rendition="#italic">deferred.</hi></p>
                <p>(9) <hi rendition="#italic">Motor Torpedo Boats</hi></p>
                <p>Decision <hi rendition="#italic">deferred.</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#flush">III. <hi rendition="#italic">Next Meeting:</hi></p>
                <p>of the Council, Monday, December 2nd, at 4 p.m.;</p>
                <p>of the Deputies, Monday, December 2nd, at 11 a.m.</p>
